  "body": "**Original comment by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nStill a problem left with these snapshots.\n\n* Open a raw or jpg, make a snapshot, call it 'loaded'\n* Adapt exposure, make a snapshot, call it ‘expo’\n* Adapt white balance \\(a lot\\), make a snapshot, call it ‘wb’.\n\nSo far, so good. \n\nNow click snapshot expo. The white balance slider goes back to its original position, but the image does not change. Only by changing the wb slider with \\+1 or -1, the original wb is back. \n\nRelated. Click snapshot loaded. The original image appears. Click expo and the adapted expo appears. Click wb, the wb slider is a lot to the right but the image does not change. Again \\+1 or -1 solves this. \n\n‌\n",
